<bold>
<italic toggle="yes">N</italic> = 158</bold>
</td></tr><tr><td style="padding-left:10%" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">P&#x02010;tau217 Pos</td><td colspan="2" align="char" rowspan="1">68 (54.8)</td><td colspan="2" align="char" rowspan="1">10 (29.4)</td><td align="char" rowspan="1" colspan="1">78 (49.4)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding-left:10%" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">P&#x02010;tau217 Ind</td><td colspan="2" align="char" rowspan="1">22 (17.7)</td><td colspan="2" align="char" rowspan="1">8 (23.5)</td><td align="char" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30 (19.0)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding-left:10%" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">P&#x02010;tau217 Neg</td><td colspan="2" align="char" rowspan="1">34 (27.4)</td><td colspan="2" align="char" rowspan="1">16 (47.1)</td><td align="char" rowspan="1" colspan="1">50 (31.7)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="dad270201-tbl2-note-0001"><p>
<italic toggle="yes">Note</italic>: All results are displayed as <italic toggle="yes">n</italic> (%).</p></fn><fn id="dad270201-tbl2-note-0002"><p>Abbreviations: AD, Alzheimer's disease; Ind, indeterminate; p&#x02010;tau, phosphorylated tau; p&#x02010;tau217&#x02013;, p&#x02010;tau217 negative; p&#x02010;tau217+, p&#x02010;tau217 positive; URG, underrepresented group.</p></fn><fn id="dad270201-tbl2-note-0003"><label>
<sup>a</sup>
</label><p>All patient analysis results are subcategorized as diagnostic certainty &#x02265;80 or diagnostic certainty &#x0003c;80.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot><permissions><copyright-holder>John Wiley &#x00026; Sons, Ltd.</copyright-holder></permissions></table-wrap></sec><sec id="dad270201-sec-0170"><label>3.3</label><title>Patient management and diagnostic confidence</title><p>A total of 85.8% (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;302) of patients in the tested arm versus 75.3% (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;140) in the untested arm had a change in a planned patient management item (Questions 3&#x02013;5) between Questionnaires A and B (<italic toggle="yes">p&#x000a0;</italic>=&#x000a0;0.0024). Change in a planned diagnostic management item was more common in the tested arm than in the untested arm (62.8%, <italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;221&#x000a0;vs 50.5%, <italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;94; <italic toggle="yes">p&#x000a0;</italic>=&#x000a0;0.0061), as was a change in a pharmacologic management item (53.1%, <italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;187&#x000a0;vs 40.3%, <italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;75; <italic toggle="yes">p&#x000a0;</italic>=&#x000a0;0.0047) and a counseling management item (48.9%, <italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;172&#x000a0;vs 36.6%, <italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;68; <italic toggle="yes">p&#x000a0;</italic>=&#x000a0;0.0063). The mean (SD) number of management items changed for patient was 3.11 (2.54) in the tested arm and 2.13 (1.95) in the untested arm (<italic toggle="yes">p&#x000a0;</italic>&#x0003c;&#x000a0;0.001; Table&#x000a0;<xref rid="dad270201-tbl-0003" ref-type="table">3</xref>). The percentage of patients for whom each of the 26 management items was added or removed, stratified by arm, is provided in Figure&#x000a0;<xref rid="dad270201-fig-0002" ref-type="fig">2</xref>. The percentage of patients in the tested arm for whom each of the 26 management items was added or removed differed based on the p&#x02010;tau217 result received (positive, negative, or indeterminate) and the consistency of that result with the baseline working diagnosis (<xref rid="dad270201-supinfo-0001" ref-type="">eFigures S2&#x02013;S4</xref>). After the 4&#x02010;week follow&#x02010;up visit, for patients with a positive or negative result, HCPs&#x02019; working diagnoses changed for 70.5% (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;86/122) of patients with a result inconsistent with the HCP's baseline working diagnosis. Change in working diagnosis was observed for 29.3% (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;103) of patients in the tested arm versus 15.6% (<italic toggle="yes">n</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;29) of patients in the untested arm (<italic toggle="yes">p&#x000a0;</italic>=&#x000a0;0.0005; Table&#x000a0;<xref rid="dad270201-tbl-0003" ref-type="table">3</xref>).</p><table-wrap position="float" id="dad270201-tbl-0003" content-type="TABLE"><label>TABLE 3</label><caption><p>Changes in patient management, working diagnosis, and diagnostic confidence at Week 4 following receipt of p&#x02010;tau217 results for the tested arm.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="char" char="(" span="1"/><col align="char" char="(" span="1"/><col align="char" char="." span="1"/><thead><tr style="border-bottom:solid 1px #000000"><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Tested arm (<italic toggle="yes">N</italic> = 352)</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Untested arm (<italic toggle="yes">N</italic> = 186)</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
